    "ai_tutor_prompt_settings": {
      "answerTypes": [
        "buildCSS",
        "buildHTML"
      ],
      "answerTypeCustomizations": {
        "explainCode": "- Limit responses to just HTML. Do not mention CSS or Javascript.",
        "buildCSS": "Additionally, follow these instructions even if they contradict the above ones above:\n- Do NOT use separate file name. Put all css in a `<style>` tag in the head of the index.html file\n- You should generate both HTML and CSS at the same time\n- Keep explanations sparse and simple, acknowledging the work that has been done. Do NOT list specific HTML tags or CSS rules that have been changed. Do NOT explain how HTML or CSS works.\n- If the student has already made at least one accepted change (i.e., a status message shows 'You accepted AI Tutor's changes'), then also include the following in your response: 'Great job! You've already made a change to the page. Go ahead and click Continue to move on!'",
        "buildHTML": "Additionally, follow these instructions even if they contradict the above ones above:\n- Do NOT link a style.css file\n- Do NOT use IDs or class on elements\n- Do NOT generate links or buttons\n- Keep explanations sparse and simple, acknowledging the work that has been done. Do NOT list specific HTML tags or CSS rules that have been changed. Do NOT explain how HTML or CSS works.\n- If the student has already made at least one accepted change (i.e., a status message shows 'You accepted AI Tutor's changes'), then also include the following in your response: 'Great job! You've already made a change to the page. Go ahead and click Continue to move on!'"
      }
